---
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Account data & privacy — Inferno Tips</title>
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="credits-page">
      <a href="/#account">← Account settings</a>
      <h1>Account data & privacy</h1>
      <p>
        Signing in is optional. You can practise without an account, with
        progress saved in your browser.
      </p>
      <h2>When you sign in</h2>
      <p>
        We use Discord to identify your account. We store your provider
        identifier, name, email, and sign-in session details in Cloudflare D1.
        Provider tokens are encrypted by the authentication library before
        storage. We do not ask for a password or access to your Discord
        messages.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your email is not shown on public leaderboards. Public scores use the
        name you choose when publishing a result.
      </p>
      <h2>Drill results and browser history</h2>
      <p>
        Signed-in drills send your prayer, movement and supply inputs to our
        server for scoring. Your account keeps the lesson, result, timing, and
        feedback. Browser history can be imported once as unverified personal
        history; it does not grant verified mastery or leaderboard scores.
      </p>
      <p>
        Completed drill summaries remain until you delete your account.
        Unfinished drill attempts expire after 30 days. The account export
        includes up to 10,000 recent attempts. Pending uploads are kept in this
        browser for retry and are not shared with another account.
      </p>
      <h2>Cookies and abuse prevention</h2>
      <p>
        We use secure cookies for sign-in and guest-score ownership. Cloudflare
        Turnstile checks requests when signing in, publishing scores, or
        deleting an account. Cloudflare processes network information to serve
        the site and reduce abuse. The app uses IP-based and account-based
        request limits.
      </p>
      <p>
        Keybinds, sound settings, and browser-only progress stay on your device.
        Clearing browser data may remove these settings and unsynced runs.
      </p>
      <h2>Your controls</h2>
      <p>
        Account settings let you export data, sign out on all devices, or
        permanently delete your account and linked public scores. Deleting an
        account does not clear browser-only progress. You can clear that
        separately under Your progress.
      </p>
      <p>
        If more sign-in providers are added, accounts will be linked only when
        you explicitly choose to link them while signed in. We do not merge
        accounts based solely on a matching email address.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">
          Cloudflare privacy policy
        </a>{' '}
        · <a href="https://discord.com/privacy">Discord privacy policy</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        This account feature is being tested in staging. Staging accounts and
        scores are separate from production.
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
